// prompt: family F5e (fil-c trust boundary, vic/notes/20261117--filc-rule-coverage__s4_design.md): user code (user(u)) may not
// define a Srs.* unit (reserved-name, s2 srs_name_forge), may not write an extern that names the bare Ptr type (ptr-outside-srs,
// fil-c FC01/02/08), and may not write an extern that names a refined Ptr type of the image (ffi-forge, fil-c FC64-66/73). Inside
// the image, pointer arithmetic and int<->pointer casts (rt_ptr_add, rt_ptr_of, rt_ptr_addr: primArith) are allowed only in the
// allocator Srs.Arena.* (ptr-arith-outside-allocator, fil-c FC51/55/56), raw word access (rt_ptr_get, rt_ptr_set: primMem) only in
// Srs.Arena.* and the globals words of Srs.Gate.* / Srs.Pages.* (ptr-access-outside-allocator), trusted code names no bare Ptr
// (raw-ptr), and rt_ptr_add has the one caller Srs.Arena.wordAdd (ptr-align: offsets are whole words, fil-c FC58-61).
def Gate.f5eRules(): Str = ".decl user(c1: number)\n.decl ptrDef(c1: number)\n.decl tref(c1: number, c2: number)\n.decl primArith(c1: number)\n.decl primMem(c1: number)\n.decl allocU(c1: number)\n.decl globU(c1: number)\n.decl primAdd(c1: number)\n.decl wordU(c1: number)\n.input user\n.input ptrDef\n.input tref\n.input primArith\n.input primMem\n.input allocU\n.input globU\n.input primAdd\n.input wordU\n.decl badReserved(c1: number)\n.decl badUserPtr(c1: number)\n.decl badFfi(c1: number)\n.decl badPtrArith(c1: number)\n.decl badPtrMem(c1: number)\n.decl badAlign(c1: number)\n.output badReserved\n.output badUserPtr\n.output badFfi\n.output badPtrArith\n.output badPtrMem\n.output badAlign\nbadReserved(u) :- user(u), srs(u).\nbadUserPtr(u) :- user(u), ext(u), ptr(u).\nbadFfi(u) :- user(u), ext(u), tref(u, v), ptrDef(v), !user(v).\nbadFfi(u) :- user(u), ext(u), ref(u, v), ptrDef(v), !user(v).\nbadPtrArith(u) :- ref(u, v), primArith(v), srs(u), !allocU(u).\nbadPtrMem(u) :- ref(u, v), primMem(v), srs(u), !allocU(u), !globU(u).\n.decl badRawPtr(c1: number)\n.output badRawPtr\nbadRawPtr(u) :- rawPtr(u), srs(u).\nbadRawPtr(u) :- rawPtr(u), ext(u), !user(u).\nbadAlign(u) :- ref(u, v), primAdd(v), srs(u), !wordU(u).\n"

